Biographical Sketch: EROZAN, Yener S. Associate Professor of Pathology Birthdate: 6-1-30 (1 of 2)

EDUCATION:	Degree/Cert.	Conferred	Field of Study
Univ.of Istanbul School of Medicine,Ist.,Turkey	M.D.	1934	Medicine
Haydiarpasa Numune Hosp.,Istanbul,Turkey	Res.(Certif.)	1959	Pathology
Suburban Hospital, Bethesda, MD	Res.(Certif.)	1962	Pathology
Johns Hopkins Univ.School of Med.,Baltimore	Fellow	1964	Cytopathology

EMPLOYMENT:

1954-1955: Medical Officer, Turkish Army;

1964-1965: Instructor in Pathology, The Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine, Baltimore, MD;
1965-1967: Instructor in Pathology, Hacattepe University School of Medicine, Ankara, Turkey;
1967-1968: Assistant Professor of Pathology, Hacettepe University School of Medicine, Ankara;
1968-1975: Assistant Professor of Pathology, The Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine;
1975-Pres: Associate Professor of Pathology, The Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine.

PERTINENT EXPERIENCE:

Hospital: 1965-1968, Pathologist, Hacettepe Medical Center, Ankara, Turkey; 1972-pres, Pathologist, The Johns Hopkins Hospital, Baltimore, Maryland;

Pertinent Consultantships: 5/16/76-6/16/76, Short-term Consultant, World Health Organization, Kancheepuram, Tamil Nadu, India;

Diplomate: 1959, Pathology Board, Turkish Ministry of Health; 6/74, American Board of Pathology; Licensure: 3/27/63, ECFMG (Standard Certificate); 1/27/72, Maryland (FLEX);

Member: American Society of Cytology, (Vice President 1983-84, President Elect, 1984-85); American

Medical Association; American Association for the Advancement of Science; International Academy of Pathology; Johns Hopkins Alumni and Faculty Association; Maryland Society of Pathologists; Founding Member, International Association for the Study of Lung Cancer;

Fellow: International Academy of Cytology; American Society of Clinical Pathologists;

President: 1985-1986, American Society of Cytology;

Research Projects: Cytopathologist, "Morphology of Lung Cancer in its Developmental and Non-

invasive Stages", Research Contracts NIH-N01-CB-92172, and NIH-N01-CN-45037; Cytopathologist, "Two-pronged Approach to Lung Cancer", Research Contract, The William Penn Foundation.

PUBLICATIONS - Past Three Years:

